(b) (i) Except as provided in Subsection (5)(b)(ii), an actor who is subject to a mandatory jail sentence under Subsection (5)(a) may not be released to the federal Immigration and Customs Enforcement Agency of the United States Department of Homeland Security for deportation until the actor has served the entire jail sentence described in Subsection (5)(a).
(ii) An actor may be released to the federal Immigration and Customs Enforcement Agency of the United States Department of Homeland Security for deportation at any time during the 14-day period before the final day of the actor''s jail sentence described in Subsection (5)(a).
(6) Notwithstanding any other provision of this section, a violation of this section is subject to the penalties and classifications under Section 76-18-204, Enhanced penalties and sentencing for certain drug offenses, if the trier of fact finds the elements described under Section 76-18-204.
